From 98dab75213f6ee66e1fcf86f858cce55cbf44313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:58:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] config: add MCP_PASSTHROUGH_HEADERS to forward listed client
 headers

Add MCP_PASSTHROUGH_HEADERS, a comma-separated list of header names to
copy from the incoming MCP HTTP request onto the requests sent to
VictoriaTraces. mcp-victorialogs and mcp-victoriametrics already have
this variable; the semantics are the same: off by default, only
effective in sse/http modes (stdio has no incoming HTTP request), names
are matched case-insensitively, entries are trimmed and empty ones
skipped.

Forwarded headers are applied after VT_INSTANCE_BEARER_TOKEN and
VT_INSTANCE_HEADERS, so a forwarded header wins on collision.
AccountID and ProjectID are still set from the tool arguments
afterwards.

This lets a deployment that fronts VictoriaTraces with an authenticating
proxy use each caller's own Authorization header instead of one shared
token.
